# Copy to .env and adjust so the app can reach your backend.
#
# - iOS simulator: http://localhost:4000 usually works.
# - Android emulator: use http://10.0.2.2:4000 (localhost on the host machine).
# - Physical phone (Expo Go): use your computer's LAN IP, e.g. http://192.168.1.23:4000
#   (phone and computer must be on the same Wi-Fi network).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# "Google ile devam et" (see src/screens/Giri.tsx and src/utils/googleAuth.ts).
# Uses the native @react-native-google-signin/google-signin SDK (Google Play
# Services) - no browser, no redirect URI or custom URI scheme to configure.
# Create OAuth client IDs at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials:
# - A "Web application" client - its ID goes in EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID
#   below AND as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID on the backend (see backend/.env.example).
#   Google always issues the ID token addressed to this Web client, even when
#   sign-in happened on Android.
# - An "Android" client, registered with this app's package name
#   (app.firevibe.sparkr) and signing certificate SHA-1. Nothing from this
#   client's ID needs to go in this file - Android resolves it automatically
#   from the package name + SHA-1 - but the client must exist in the same
#   Google Cloud project as the Web client above, or sign-in will fail.
# - An "iOS" client, registered with this app's bundle id
#   (app.firevibe.sparkr, see app.json's ios.bundleIdentifier). Its Client ID
#   goes in EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID below. IMPORTANT: iOS also needs
#   that client's REVERSED id (Google Cloud Console shows it right under the
#   client, formatted like com.googleusercontent.apps.XXXXXXXXXX-yyyyyyyyyy)
#   pasted into app.json's "@react-native-google-signin/google-signin" plugin
#   entry as { "iosUrlScheme": "<that value>" } - without it, the native
#   sign-in sheet opens but can never redirect back into the app.
# Leave EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID empty to keep the button showing a
# "not configured yet" message instead of a broken sign-in attempt.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# RevenueCat (see src/utils/subscription.ts) - powers Premium/Boost/Super
# Vibe pack purchases on both platforms through one shared paywall. Create a
# project at app.revenuecat.com, then add an "App Store" app (needs your
# App Store Connect app + its in-app purchase shared secret) and a
# "Play Store" app (needs your Google Play service account JSON) inside it -
# each gets its OWN API key below; they are NOT interchangeable between
# platforms. Leave either empty to keep that platform's paywall showing a
# clear "not configured" state instead of a silent crash.
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=
